        <senderName>Environment Canada</senderName>
        <headline>red warning - tornado - in effect</headline>
        <description>
At 9:21 p.m. CST, Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible.

Tornado Location:  About 20 km southeast of Rabbit Lake

Golf ball to tennis ball sized hail is falling with this storm.

Motion:  Moving southeast at 45 km/h

Locations in the Path:
Mullingar
Mayfair
Alticane
Keatley
Hafford

###

This is a very dangerous and potentially life-threatening situation.

Tornadoes at night cannot be seen and may strike suddenly. Sometimes they are preceded by strengthening winds, large hail, or an approaching whistling or roaring sound. Tornado warnings are issued when a thunderstorm is producing or is likely to produce a tornado.
</description>
        <instruction>
Take cover immediately in a basement, interior room, or a sturdy shelter when threatening weather approaches. If no shelter is available, lie in a low spot and protect your head from flying debris. If you are out on the water when threatening weather approaches, return to shore and seek shelter, if possible. Otherwise, move away from the path of the tornado to escape. Wear your lifejacket, lie face down  and protect your head.
</instruction>
        <web>https://weather.gc.ca/</web>
